Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• `posts_questions.id`: primary key for each question; join target for answers (`parent_id`) and for comments (`post_id` when the comment is on a question).  
• `posts_questions.tags`: the tag string (e.g. `<java><spring>`); this is the value we ultimately want to report.  
• `posts_questions.owner_user_id`: the author‑user of the question; filter to the required user‑id range.  
• `posts_questions.creation_date`: date the question was asked; filter to 2019‑07‑01 … 2019‑12‑31.  

• `posts_answers.id`: primary key for every answer; join target for comments (`post_id` when the comment is on an answer).  
• `posts_answers.parent_id`: the question id the answer belongs to – bridge to the tags we need.  
• `posts_answers.owner_user_id`: the answer author; filter to the required user‑id range.  
• `posts_answers.creation_date`: date the answer was posted; filter to the date window.  

• `comments.id`: primary key for each comment.  
• `comments.post_id`: id of the post (question *or* answer) the comment is attached to.  
• `comments.user_id`: the commenter’s user id; filter to the required user‑id range.  
• `comments.creation_date`: date the comment was made; filter to the date window.  

Constant filter conditions used again and again  

```
WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'      -- inclusive / exclusive
  AND user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
```  

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory / building‑block queries  
(Each one returns at most 20 rows so you can quickly inspect the data.)  
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at questions asked by the user cohort in the period
SELECT id AS question_id,
       owner_user_id,
       tags,
       creation_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Same as #1 but only the DISTINCT tag strings
SELECT DISTINCT tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Answers written by the user cohort during the period
SELECT id AS answer_id,
       parent_id AS question_id,
       owner_user_id,
       creation_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`
WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Tags of the question that each answer (from #3) belongs to
SELECT a.owner_user_id,
       a.id            AS answer_id,
       q.id            AS question_id,
       q.tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`   AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
  ON q.id = a.parent_id
WHERE a.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND a.owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Comments *directly* on questions by the user cohort
SELECT c.id            AS comment_id,
       c.user_id,
       q.id            AS question_id,
       q.tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.comments`        AS c
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
  ON q.id = c.post_id
WHERE c.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND c.user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Comments on answers (need two joins to reach the question’s tags)
SELECT c.id            AS comment_id,
       c.user_id,
       a.id            AS answer_id,
       q.id            AS question_id,
       q.tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.comments`        AS c
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`   AS a
  ON a.id = c.post_id                       -- comment is on an answer
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
  ON q.id = a.parent_id                     -- answer’s parent question
WHERE c.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND c.user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Union of the three contribution types (questions, answers, comments on Q)
--    Reduced to two columns (user_id, tags) for brevity
SELECT owner_user_id AS user_id, tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208

UNION ALL
SELECT a.owner_user_id AS user_id, q.tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`   AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
  ON q.id = a.parent_id
WHERE a.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND a.owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208

UNION ALL
SELECT c.user_id, q.tags
FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.comments`        AS c
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
  ON q.id = c.post_id
WHERE c.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
  AND c.user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Same as #7, but adds the “comment‑on‑answer” path too
SELECT user_id, tags FROM (
  -- questions written
  SELECT owner_user_id AS user_id, tags
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
  WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208

  UNION ALL
  -- answers written
  SELECT a.owner_user_id AS user_id, q.tags
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`   AS a
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
    ON q.id = a.parent_id
  WHERE a.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND a.owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208

  UNION ALL
  -- comments on questions
  SELECT c.user_id, q.tags
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.comments`        AS c
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
    ON q.id = c.post_id
  WHERE c.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND c.user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208

  UNION ALL
  -- comments on answers
  SELECT c.user_id, q.tags
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.comments`        AS c
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`   AS a
    ON a.id = c.post_id
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
    ON q.id = a.parent_id
  WHERE c.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND c.user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Break the <tag><tag2> string into individual tag tokens for one slice
SELECT user_id,
       t AS single_tag
FROM (
  SELECT owner_user_id AS user_id,
         REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(tags, r'<([^>]+)>') AS tag_array
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
  WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
  LIMIT 20
), UNNEST(tag_array) AS t;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final (comprehensive) answer: user_id + individual tag token
SELECT user_id,
       single_tag
FROM (
  /* build a UNION of all contribution paths */
  SELECT owner_user_id AS user_id, tags
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions`
  WHERE creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208

  UNION ALL
  SELECT a.owner_user_id AS user_id, q.tags
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`   AS a
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
    ON q.id = a.parent_id
  WHERE a.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND a.owner_user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208

  UNION ALL
  SELECT c.user_id, q.tags
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.comments`        AS c
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
    ON q.id = c.post_id
  WHERE c.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND c.user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208

  UNION ALL
  SELECT c.user_id, q.tags
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.comments`        AS c
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_answers`   AS a
    ON a.id = c.post_id
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.stackoverflow.posts_questions` AS q
    ON q.id = a.parent_id
  WHERE c.creation_date BETWEEN '2019-07-01' AND '2020-01-01'
    AND c.user_id BETWEEN 16712208 AND 18712208
) AS all_contribs,
UNNEST(REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(tags, r'<([^>]+)>')) AS single_tag
LIMIT 20;
```

The sequence shows how to reach and verify every required component, from simple inspection queries to a complete solution delivering the requested `(user_id, tag)` pairs for all contributions in the specified six‑month window.
